            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of William Shockley</strong><br>\nWilliam Shockley was born in London, England, in 1910. His parents were Americans, and his family moved back to the United States when he was three years old. He grew up in California where he showed early interest in science and engineering. Shockley was an exceptional student, which earned him a scholarship to the California Institute of Technology, where he began his studies in physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Early Career</strong><br>\nAfter earning his bachelor's degree from the California Institute of Technology, Shockley went on to pursue his Ph.D. at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT). His doctoral thesis focused on the energy states of electrons in solid materials, a topic that would serve as a foundation for his later work on semiconductors and transistors.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Bell Labs Years</strong><br>\nIn 1936, Shockley joined Bell Labs, a leading research company in communication technology. There, he worked on various research projects, including the development of radar technology during World War II. Shockley's expertise in solid-state physics was critical to the war effort and laid the groundwork for his post-war research.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
