          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Controversial Views on Intelligence</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Shockley became a controversial figure due to his public views on intelligence and genetics. He advocated for eugenics and proposed that individuals with lower IQs should be discouraged from reproducing. These views were widely criticized by the scientific community and the public.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Modern Electronics</strong><br>\nDespite the controversy, Shockley's contribution to modern electronics remains undisputed. His work on the transistor has had a lasting impact, with its applications seen in almost every modern electronic device. The world of computing and communication technology owes much to Shockley's invention.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nWilliam Shockley died in 1989, leaving behind a complex legacy. He is remembered both for his scientific achievements and his controversial opinions on genetics and intelligence. Shockley's contributions to the field of electronics continue to influence technological innovation and development.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
